# Halo: Combat Evolved (4D530004), Nova. Built from the generic survey
# 1790933948-titleroutes-171581 (lane.titleroutes session 65, read by
# lane.titleroutes2 session 1, 2026-10-02). Read from its route-frames,
# not guessed:
#   boot20 (031011): the Bungie logo; boot40/booted (031032, 031054): the
#     main menu, CAMPAIGN lit.
#   cycle 1 (031100 START / 031106 A): START picks CAMPAIGN -> ENTER NAME
#     with the default "New001" and the cursor on Done; A takes it ->
#     CHOOSE DIFFICULTY, NORMAL lit.
#   cycle 2 (031111 START / 031117 A): START picks Normal -> LOADING; black.
#   cycle 3 (031123 START / 031129 A): black, then "Reveille": the cryo bay,
#     the tech at his console. Live and player-controlled.
#   cycles 4-14: START opens the pause panel (RESUME GAME lit; objective
#     "Complete training diagnostic") and A resumes. The tip "Use RIGHT
#     [stick] to look around" stays up the whole time: the look training
#     waits for up/down look input, and the survey only ever sent RX.
#   play (031405-031456): the same room with the camera swung right.
# So: 5 START/A cycles (3 reached the cryo bay; 2 guard pairs are pause +
# resume), then a training block that looks up, down, left and right on
# the RIGHT stick and walks on the LEFT stick, three times over (so the
# training's order does not matter), mark, then a walk loop with no START.
# A is jump and X is action in play; B (melee) and A also answer an
# "invert the look?" question either way, which does not change the run.
# The survey made a "New001" profile; if the title now lists profiles
# first, START/A pick the lit one, so the cycle count should hold -- the
# frames will say. What a pass looks like: the play frames leave the cryo
# bay (corridors of the Pillar of Autumn), not five minutes of one room.
# Replay 1 (1790940485-titleroutes2-1612232, ref 685c52e514): no ROUTE
# FAIL; SELECT PROFILE (New001) -> LOAD LEVEL (The Pillar of Autumn) ->
# CHOOSE DIFFICULTY -> the cryo bay on cycle 4; the training block cleared
# the look test, and the mark (045315) came with "Use X to exit the
# cryo-tube" still up; the walk loop's X took it. The rest of the window
# was the cryo bay under "Stand on the red square", wandering (static 0.0,
# 99% at 30+): live, but the scripted walk never started.
# HELD Nova nav session (lane.titleroutes2 s1, 05:19-05:35 PDT,
# ~/hakux-work/nav/halo-ce.returning-20261002T051941/, 59 frames) found the
# rest of the calibration, in order:
#   1. look test ("Use RIGHT to look around") -- any up/down look;
#   2. "Use X to exit the cryo-tube" (X, not A), then a short cutscene;
#      control returns facing the tube row, the tech to the right, the red
#      square on the floor beside him;
#   3. "Use LEFT to move / RIGHT to look", then stepping onto the red
#      square in front of the light pillar;
#   4. "Target each of the flashing lights": five lights in a cross on the
#      pillar (centre, top, left, right, bottom), each turns green when the
#      crosshair sits on it; then the same five again with "Vertical
#      looking is now inverted";
#   5. "Press B to try it the other way / Press A to leave it like it is":
#      A; a GAMEPLAY HELP panel that A does NOT close and START does;
#      "Checkpoint... done". Nothing else happened in the next ~2 min.
# Step 4 needs aimed input: the right stick is very fast at full throw (a
# ~0.4 s tap turns ~90 degrees), a third-throw (RX 16000) tap moves ~25 px,
# two-thirds (22000) ~65 px; vertical taps at full throw ~160 px. An
# open-loop route would have to replay the walk to the square and ten
# aimed taps exactly; that is a drive.py (screen-aware) job, or a save
# made after the checkpoint. This file is a DRAFT that reaches the cryo
# bay only.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
shot booted
repeat 5 {
    press START
    wait 5
    shot menu-start
    press A
    wait 5
    shot menu-a
}
repeat 3 {
    axis RY min
    wait 1.5
    axis RY mid
    wait 2
    axis RY max
    wait 1.5
    axis RY mid
    wait 2
    axis RX max
    wait 0.8
    axis RX mid
    wait 1
    axis RX min
    wait 0.8
    axis RX mid
    wait 1
    press B
    wait 2
    axis LY min
    wait 2
    axis LY mid
    wait 2
    shot training
}
mark gameplay               # CHECK: player control past the look training, no pause panel
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 4
    press X
    wait 0.5
    axis RX max
    wait 0.5
    axis RX mid
    wait 3
    press A
    wait 1
    axis RX min
    wait 0.9
    axis RX mid
    wait 3
    axis LY mid
    axis LX max
    wait 1
    axis LX mid
    axis LY min
    wait 3
    axis LY mid
    shot play
}
